    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d316">

                <pb facs="0382" n="332" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg332"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr.
                            Arriaga.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-09-20"><hi rendition="#italic">September 20,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to our conversation this
                    forenoon, I have the honor to inform you that the so-called reciprocity
                    arrangement between the United States and Guatemala was based on the third
                    section of the statute known as the McKinley law, which was repealed by the
                    going into effect of our existing tariff law, at midnight on the 27th
                    ultimo.</p>
                <p>This is in accordance with the opinion of the Secretary of the Treasury, in which
                    I concur.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
